OK   the channel reads the new refresh token: ["ACTIVE",true]
OK   auth status probes with the new grant: [200,"AUTHORIZED"]
OK   the status probe used the new refresh token, not the old one: true
NOTE the old refresh token at the provider after re-authorization (still live = not revoked there): {"oldTokenStillLiveAtProvider":true,"revokeCallsToProvider":0}
FAIL vault.remove with the wrong purpose refuses and keeps the value: ["TypeError","ACTIVE"] (expected ["CredentialPurposeError","ACTIVE"])
FAIL vault.remove of an unknown reference is harmless (false): "TypeError" (expected false)

